// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
// compare.py's arguments and help (mise run text:compare --help). mise rewraps the help to the
// terminal but keeps its line breaks: a paragraph, or a list's item, is one line.

long_about """
    Our page of a version against EUR-Lex's HTML of it, as a reader sees both: line by line.

    The reference is the version's xhtml manifestation in Cellar, by the CELEX the page shows: the HTML EUR-Lex shows (its site answers scripts with a JavaScript challenge; Cellar is its interface for machines). It is fetched once into text-compare/reference/ (ignored by git and Bazel), and shown with scripts off, styled as EUR-Lex styles it: its stylesheets are behind the same challenge, so they are the Internet Archive's copies (STYLESHEETS), fetched once too, the text in EUR-Lex's frame (FRAME).

    Both pages are read in a headless Chromium, the same width: a line is the text of a block (a paragraph, a heading, a cell), and blocks side by side (a table's row, a number beside its heading) are one line. The lines are aligned, and each difference is sorted into a kind:

    - missing: a line of EUR-Lex's that we don't show
    - extra: a line of ours that EUR-Lex doesn't have
    - moved: the same line, elsewhere
    - split: one line of EUR-Lex's that we show as several (the same text)
    - merged: several of EUR-Lex's that we show as one
    - regrouped: the same text, broken into lines differently
    - spacing: the same line but for spaces
    - marker: the same line but for what starts or ends it (a list's dash, a number)
    - changed: a line whose text differs
    - aligned: the same line, set elsewhere across the column (left, centred, right, or indented)
    - styled: the same line in another face (bold, italic)

    The differences are then grouped into patterns, by kind and by the elements that made the lines (EUR-Lex's classes, ours: each legal-text element's template writes its name as a class): one pattern is one thing to fix. The patterns are printed, most frequent first, with an example each; text-compare/reports/{celex}.md lists every difference.
    """

arg "<page>..." help="A version's page: http://127.0.0.1:8080/eli/…/{date}/{language}"

example "mise run text:compare http://127.0.0.1:8080/eli/reg_impl/2015/1998/2015-11-15/eng" header="Compare a page with EUR-Lex" help="Differences sorted into kinds and grouped into patterns"
example "mise run text:compare http://127.0.0.1:8080/eli/reg_impl/2015/1998/2015-11-15/eng http://127.0.0.1:8080/eli/dir/2009/28/2015-10-05/eng" header="Compare several pages" help="One after another; reports in text-compare/reports/{celex}.md"
